{
  "title": "Bidding Farewell (Wida) to the Holy Imams (a.s.)",
  "data": "When you are about to leave the shrine of any of the Imams (a.s.), bid farewell at the tomb with:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَهْلَ بَيْتِ النُّبُوَّةِ وَمَعْدِنَ الرِّسَالَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA AHLA BAYTIN NUBUWWATI WA MA'DINAR RISAALAH\nPeace be upon you all, O household of prophethood and essence of the (divine) Message.\nسَلَامَ مُوَدِّعٍ لَا سَئِمٍ وَلَا قَالٍ\nSALAAMA MUWADDI'IN LAA SA'IMIN WA LAA QAAL\nI offer you the salutation of one who has to bid farewell to you although he is neither bored with you nor tired of you.\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ اِنَّهٗ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUHOO A'LAYKUM AHLAL BAYTI INNAHOO HAMEEDUN MAJEED\nAllah's mercy and blessings be upon you, O People of the Household. He is verily worthy of praise, full of glory.\nسَلَامَ وَلِيٍّ غَيْرِ رَاغِبٍ عَنْكُمْ\nSALAAMA WALIYYIN GHAYRI RAAGHIBIN A'NKUM\n[I greet you] with the greeting of a loyalist to you who never forsakes you,\nوَلَا مُنْحَرِفٍ عَنْكُمْ وَلَا مُسْتَبْدِلٍ بِكُمْ\nWA LAA MUNHARIFIN A'NKUM WA LAA MUSTABDILIN BIKUM\nnever deviates from you, never substitutes you,\nوَلَا مُؤْثِرٍ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَا زَاهِدٍ فِيْ قُرْبِكُمْ\nWA LAA MU'THIRIN A'LAYKUM WA LAA ZAAHIDIN FEE QURBIKUM\nnever chooses others than you, and never becomes weary of being in your vicinity.\nلَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَةِ قُبُوْرِكُمْ وَاِتْيَانِ مَشَاهِدِكُمْ\nLAA JA'ALAHULLAAHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN ZIYAARATI QUBOORIKUM WA ITYAANI MASHAAHIDIKUM\nMay Allah never decide this time to be my last visit to your tombs and coming to your shrines.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM\nPeace be upon you all.\nوَحَشَرَنِيَ اللّٰهُ فِي زُمْرَتِكُمْ وَاَوْرَدَنِيْ حَوْضَكُمْ\nWA HASHARANIYALLAAHU FEE ZUMRATIKUM WA AWRADANEE HAWDAKUM\nMay Allah include me with your group, allow me to come to your pond,\nوَاَرْضَاكُمْ عَنِّيْ وَمَكَّنَنِيْ فِيْ دَوْلَتِكُمْ\nWA ARDAAKUM A'NNEE WA MAKKANANEE FEE DAWLATIKUM\nmake you to be pleased with me, give me authority in your (expected) government,\nوَاَحْيَانِيْ فِيْ رَجْعَتِكُمْ وَمَلَّكَنِيْ فِيْۤ اَيَّامِكُمْ\nWA AHYAANEE FEE RAJ'ATIKUM WA MALLAKANEE FEE AYYAAMIKUM\nrestore me to life at your Return, grant me power on the days of your authority,\nوَشَكَرَ سَعْيِيْ لَكُمْ وَغَفَرَ ذُنُوْبِيْ بِشَفَاعَتِكُمْ\nWA SHAKARA SA'YEE LAKUM WA GHAFARA DHUNOOBEE BISHAFAA'ATIKUM\nthank my efforts for visiting you, forgive my sins through your intercession,\nوَاَقَالَ عَثْرَتِيْ بِحُبِّكُمْ وَاَعْلٰى كَعْبِيْ بِمُوَالَاتِكُمْ\nWA AQAALA A'THRATEE BIHUBBIKUM WA A'LAA KA'BEE BIMUWAALAATIKUM\nabsolve my slips on account of my love for you, raise my rank on account of my loyalty to you,\nوَشَرَّفَنِيْ بِطَاعَتِكُمْ وَاَعَزَّنِيْ بِهُدَاكُمْ\nWA SHARRAFANEE BITAA'ATIKUM WA A'AZZANEE BIHUDAAKUM\nendue me with honor due to my obedience to you, grant me dignity due to my following your right guidance,\nوَجَعَلَنِيْ مِمَّنْ يَنْقَلِبُ مُفْلِحًا مُنْجِحًا سَالِمًا غَانِمًا\nWA JA'ALANEE MIMMAN YANQALIBU MUFLIHAN MUNJIHAN SAALIMAN GHAANIMAA\nmake me of those who return home with success, prosperity, safety, profits,\nمُعَافًى غَنِيًّا فَاۤئِزًا بِرِضْوَانِ اللّٰهِ وَفَضْلِهٖ وَكِفَايَتِهٖ\nMU'AAFAN GHANIYYAN FAA'IZAN BIRIDWAANILLAAHI WA FADLIHEE WA KIFAAYATIH\nwellbeing, riches, and winning of Allah’s pleasure, favors, and security\nبِاَفْضَلِ مَا يَنْقَلِبُ بِهٖ اَحَدٌ مِنْ زُوَّارِكُمْ وَمَوَالِيْكُمْ وَمُحِبِّيْكُمْ وَشِيْعَتِكُمْ\nBI-AFDALI MAA YANQALIBU BIHEE AHADUN MIN ZUWWAARIKUM WA MAWAALEEKUM WA MUHIBBEEKUM WA SHEE'ATIKUM\nwith the most favorable thing that any of your visitors, loyalists, lovers, and adherents may return with.\nوَرَزَقَنِيَ اللّٰهُ الْعَوْدَ ثُمَّ الْعَوْدَ ثُمَّ الْعَوْدَ مَاۤ اَبْقَانِيْ رَبِّيْ\nWA RAZAQANIYALLAAHUL A'WDA THUMMAL A'WDA THUMMAL A'WDA MAA ABQAANEE RABBEE\nMay Allah grant me more and more chances to re-visit you, as long as my Lord keeps me alive,\nبِنِيَّةٍ صَادِقَةٍ وَاِيْمَانٍ وَتَقْوٰى وَاِخْبَاتٍ وَرِزْقٍ وَاسِعٍ حَلَالٍ طَيِّبٍ\nBINIYYATIN SAADIQATIN WA EEMAANIN WA TAQWAA WA IKHBAATIN WA RIZQIN WAASI'IN HALAALIN TAYYIB\nbearing honest intention, faith, piety, submission, and sustenance that is expansive, legally gotten, and pleasant.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِهِمْ وَذِكْرِهِمْ وَالصَّلٰوةِ عَلَيْهِمْ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN ZIYAARATIHIM WA DHIKRIHIM WAS SALAATI A'LAYHIM\nO Allah, do not decide this time to be my last visit to them, mentioning them, and invoking blessings upon them.\nوَاَوْجِبْ لِيَ الْمَغْفِرَةَ وَالرَّحْمَةَ وَالْخَيْرَ وَالْبَرَكَةَ وَالنُّوْرَ وَالْاِيْمَانَ وَحُسْنَ الْاِجَابَةِ\nWA AWJIB LIYAL MAGHFIRATA WAR RAHMATA WAL KHAYRA WAL BARAKATA WAN NOORA WAL EEMAANA WA HUSNAL IJAABAH\nMake inevitable forgiveness, mercy, goodness, blessing, light, faith, and excellent response for me,\nكَمَاۤ اَوْجَبْتَ لِاَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ الْعَارِفِيْنَ بِحَقِّهِمُ الْمُوْجِبِيْنَ طَاعَتَهُمْ\nKAMAA AWJABTA LI-AWLIYAA'IKAL A'ARIFEENA BIHAQQIHIMUL MOOJIBEENA TAA'ATAHUM\njust as You have made inevitable all that for Your intimate servants who recognize their actual status, who made obedience to them to be obligatory upon themselves,\nوَالرَّاغِبِيْنَ فِيْ زِيَارَتِهِمُ الْمُتَقَرِّبِيْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِلَيْهِمْ\nWAR RAAGHIBEENA FEE ZIYAARATIHIMUL MUTAQARRIBEENA ILAYKA WA ILAYHIM\nwho have desire to visit them, and who seek nearness to You and to them.\nبِاَبِيْۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاُمِّيْ وَنَفْسِيْ وَمَالِيْ وَاَهْلِيْ\nBI-ABEE ANTUM WA UMMEE WA NAFSEE WA MAALEE WA AHLEE\nMay my father, mother, soul, property, and family members be ransoms for you.\nاِجْعَلُوْنِيْ مِنْ هَمِّكُمْ وَصَيِّرُوْنِيْ فِيْ حِزْبِكُمْ\nIJ'ALOONEE MIN HAMMIKUM WA SAYYIROONEE FEE HIZBIKUM\n(Please, O my masters,) make me one of your concerns, make me join your party,\nوَاَدْخِلُوْنِيْ فِيْ شَفَاعَتِكُمْ وَاذْكُرُوْنِيْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ\nWA ADKHILOONEE FEE SHAFAA'ATIKUM WADHKUROONEE I'NDA RABBIKUM\ninclude me with your intercession, and remember me before your Lord.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَاَبْلِغْ اَرْوَاحَهُمْ وَاَجْسَادَهُمْ عَنِّيْ تَحِيَّةً كَثِيْرَةً وَسَلَامًا\nWA ABLIGH ARWAAHAHUM WA AJSAADAHUM A'NNEE TAHIYYATAN KATHEERATAN WA SALAAMAA\nand convey to their souls and bodies many greetings and salutations.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you all.",
  "merits": "Bidding farewell is one of the etiquettes of ziyarat: a pilgrim about to set off for home takes leave of the Imam he has visited with a farewell reported from the Imams (a.s.), and most forms of ziyarat end with one of their own.\n\nThis general farewell, which serves for any of the Imams, is reported by Shaykh Muhammad al-Mashhadi in al-Mazar al-Kabir, in its chapter on bidding farewell, and by Sayyid Ibn Tawus in Misbah al-Za'ir after the comprehensive ziyarat known as the Ziyarat of the Imams of the Believers ([The Comprehensive Ziyarat of the Imams (a.s.)](G30)). Mafatih al-Jinan quotes it from Misbah al-Za'ir."
}
